#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/contour.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.contour.contour:87
msgid ""
"[*type*]\\ *pen*\\ [**+c**\\ [**l**\\|\\ **f**]]. *type*, if present, can be "
"**a** for annotated contours or **c** for regular contours [Default]. The "
"pen sets the attributes for the particular line. Default pen for annotated "
"contours is ``\"0.75p,black\"`` and for regular contours ``\"0.25p,"
"black\"``. Normally, all contours are drawn with a fixed color determined by "
"the pen setting. If **+cl** is appended the colors of the contour lines are "
"taken from the CPT (see ``levels``). If **+cf** is appended the colors from "
"the CPT file are applied to the contour annotations. Select **+c** for both "
"effects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/contour.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.contour.contour:97
msgid ""
"Add a legend entry for the contour being plotted. Normally, the annotated "
"contour is selected for the legend. You can select the regular contour "
"instead, or both of them, by considering the label to be of the format "
"[*annotcontlabel*][/*contlabel*]. If either label contains a slash (/) "
"character then use ``|`` as the separator for the two labels instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/contour.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.contour.contour:105
msgid ""
"*projcode*\\[*projparams*/]\\ *width*\\|\\ *scale*. Select map :doc:"
"`projection </projections/index>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/contour.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.contour.contour:107
msgid ""
"[*xmin*, *xmax*, *ymin*, *ymax*] or *xmin/xmax/ymin/ymax*\\ [**+r**]"
"[**+u**\\ *unit*]. Specify the :doc:`region </tutorials/basics/regions>` of "
"interest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/contour.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.contour.contour:112
msgid ""
"Set frame and axes attributes for the plot. It can be a bool, ``\"none\"``, "
"a :class:`pygmt.params.Frame` or :class:`pygmt.params.Axis` object. Raw GMT "
"strings or sequences of strings are also supported for backward "
"compatibility. If ``frame=True``, the frame will be drawn with the default "
"attributes. If ``frame=\"none\"``, no frame will be drawn. Use a :class:"
"`pygmt.params.Frame` or :class:`pygmt.params.Axis` object for more control "
"over the attributes of the frame and axes. A tutorial is available at :doc:"
"`frame and axes attributes </tutorials/basics/frames>`. Full documentation "
"is at :gmt-docs:`gmt.html#b-full`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/contour.py:docstring
